<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Halberstadt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Halberstadt is a town north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Made a bishopric around 804 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, it was ruled by prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> gave it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in 1648. Its Gothic cathedral holds one of the richest church treasuries in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/halberstadt.jpg" alt="Halberstadt" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: marsupium photography · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Halberstadt_Dom_2023.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
